    "created_at": "2026-09-02T12:19:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-02T12:19:56Z",
    "body": "> How is it a dupe? They are different APIs. Also, WebKit implements this as specified, but I suppose we can change it.\n\nI meant that it's the same notion that those document origins are not observable, and doing this for `parseHTML` originated from the `DOMParser` API decision, so it's probably one decision for both APIs.\n\nI think it's more useful to spec the Gecko/blink implementation rather than the other way around (why throw exceptions when we don't have to).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
